Z||000000||fierobaby||06-21-2001||12:00 PM||||Hey all, I know this is an odd question but does anyone know where I can get a cheap factory sunroof seal? I looked at the Fiero store and they are $70 well I don't have that kinda cash I owe my parents almost $2000 on the car as it is! anyone know someone who has a dead Fiero and not going to fix it and will sell me the seal...well thanks guys love yall!!!<P>Corinne<P>------------------<BR>1984 Sweet Candy Apple red Fiero sport coupe :-D<BR>[IMG] [URL=http://feiro.nl/uploads/cfiero1.html [/IMG]||||reg||10
Z||000001||ROB MAC||06-21-2001||03:07 PM||||The cheapest one comes in a tube. Seal it with silicone and never breathe engine fumes again. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||PAUL88GT||06-21-2001||04:16 PM||||The seal is about $45 from <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com." TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com.</A>   However, do a search on this topic. Your problem may not be the seal, but the plastic bushings in the sunroof glass.  These bushings are cheap and easy to replace.  I would replace those first and see it it still leaks. You can get the bushings from the Pontiac dealer. <BR>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierohoho||06-21-2001||05:20 PM||||Another fix I learned from RAREW66 is to clean the seal with "Bleech White" tire cleaner and then coat the seal with vasoline and let sit overnite. The vasoline will be absorbed by the seal causing it to soften up and swell up a little. I tried this and it helped.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierobaby||06-21-2001||05:40 PM||||well Its not the bushings...there is no seal on the roof at all so I know it isn't the bushings all though we are replacing those||||reg||1
